<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's MKB to cut prime rate to 21.50 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary's MKB to cut prime rate to 21.50 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Magyar Kulkereskedelmi Bank Rt (MKB) will cut its prime lending rate on forint loans to 21.5 percent from 22.4 percent, effective April 1, 1997, the bank said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>MKB is majority owned by Germany's Bayerische Landesbank Girozentrale.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
